course: dictionary
lesson: 11623
title: Close enough: approximations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An approximation is a value that is close to the exact one but not exactly right. We use approximations when the exact answer is hard to write down or when a rough idea is enough. «The bus takes about 20 minutes» is an approximation: it is close to the real time, but it is not exact.
explain: In maths, we often round numbers to make them easier to use. π is 3.14159... and it goes on forever, so we write π ≈ 3.14. The sign ≈ means "is approximately equal to". Writing 3.14 is an approximation of π, not the whole number.
explain: An approximation can also mean something that is like something else but not exactly the same. «The drawing is a good approximation of the castle» means it looks very much like the castle, but it is not the real castle. Phrases like «a rough approximation» show a quick guess, and «a good approximation» shows a very close one.
fact: An approximation is close to the exact value but not exactly right.
fact: The sign ≈ means "approximately equal to".
fact: «π ≈ 3.14» is an approximation, because π never ends and never repeats.
fact: Scientists write measurements as approximations, because no measuring tool is perfectly exact.
fact: «A rough approximation» is a quick guess; «a good approximation» is very close to the exact answer.
exercise: What is an approximation? | *A value that is close to the exact one but not exactly right | A word that is spelt wrongly | A very long sum | A value that is exactly right every time
exercise: What does the sign ≈ mean? | Is smaller than | Is bigger than | *Is approximately equal to | Is exactly equal to
exercise: «The drawing is a good approximation of the castle.» What does this tell you? | It is the real castle | *It looks very close to the castle but is not the real thing | It is a photo of a different castle | It is a rough sketch that does not look like the castle at all
test: «The jar holds about 500 millilitres.» Is 500 millilitres an approximation or an exact amount? | A type of jar | An exact amount | *An approximation | A made-up word
test: Which is the best rounded approximation of 9.8? | 98 | *10 | 0.98 | 8
exam: Maya says her answer of 30 is an approximation of 29.6. Is she right? | *Yes, 30 is close to 29.6 but not exactly right | No, 30 is exactly right | Yes, because 30 is an exact answer | No, 30 is far too big to be close
